# wear/man/poncho_cape: the poncho's drape, over the shoulders and both arms to the hips (drawn on the near arm's layer
# above the arm, so the arms swing hidden under it), the head-hole's short slit in front, folds falling over the arms,
# a band of the trim colour across its skirt, a shallow point before and behind with a fringe along its edge; it does not sway; it lies flat over the
# body of a fallen man. The trims are the garment's edge (a border or embroidery recolours them).
# GARB-M (P2b wave 2); fitted to the man (STYLE_P2 22). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body man
role garment poncho
layer armNear
anchor neck
keys torso
z 5

